  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "A man nearly two miles tall appeared in the desert. A charter pilot found him in June 1998, scratched into a plateau in outback South Australia.",
        "visual_query": "outback south australia plateau",
        "visual_fallback": "red desert"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The lines run 28 kilometres, up to 35 metres wide, a foot deep. Satellite images show the whole figure appeared in under two weeks.",
        "visual_query": "red desert aerial outback",
        "visual_fallback": "desert aerial"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Anonymous faxes steered reporters to it, calling the figure Stuart's Giant and quoting an American book. Who builds this, then hides?",
        "visual_query": "australian desert dirt road",
        "visual_fallback": "dusty track"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Suspicion settled on Bardius Goldberg, an Alice Springs artist who worked at scale and understood GPS. Friends said he admitted it to them.",
        "visual_query": "alice springs desert town",
        "visual_fallback": "outback town"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Goldberg died in 2002 without ever confirming it, and a five thousand dollar reward in 2018 produced nobody. The grader marks are still there.",
        "visual_query": "arid australian salt plain",
        "visual_fallback": "dry plain"
      }
    ],
